Two deaths, actually:

2) Byron the healer was running a very successful protection racket. 
I won't bore you with the details; just take my word that he had good
stuff and killer AC from carrying all the random useless items from
every level above Minetown down into the shops to sell.  He walked
into a hardware store...and the shopkeeper refused to let him out
again.  Warning to fellow Nethack players: 3x3 shops are deathtraps. 
Avoid at all costs! (Well, unless you can teleport out.)

2) Cajeput the monk was running around with his dog when he found "ad
aerium" written in the dust.  Soon, he had dropped all his gold and
jumped on the teleporter to find...an empty vault?  There was a hole
in the wall, so he went outside and found a rock mole that must have
been generated inside the vault.  Disappointed that he would not be
getting any gold, he went back inside the vault and waited for the
guard to arrive (the tunnel dug by the rock mole didn't go anywhere). 
The guard arrived and Cajeput managed to get two squares from the
vault when the guard hit the rock mole's tunnel, sealed up the vault
wall and disappeared, leaving poor Cajeput stuck in a tiny space with
no way out and only a few boulders to keep him company.  But wait! 
That's not all!  He had a few unID'd scrolls in his pack, so he read
one and discovered that it was genocide.  "Arch-lichs," he said
thinking he might as well take advantage of the opportunity.  The
scroll was cursed.  Man, I am soooo glad that one didn't leave a bones
file...

